<!-- awf:section guide-authority -->
## What binds you in the agent guide, and what does not

The invariants, conventions, and commands in the repository's agent guide bind you. Its skill
catalog and workflow-chain routing do not bind you: invoke no workflow skill, create or resume no effort,
and write to no working-memory file.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section green-obligation -->
## Focused feedback

Run only focused tests and checks relevant to the bounded task. Iterating on failures is the work.
Never weaken an assertion, golden, fixture, or check to hide a failure. Name every legitimate golden
or fixture update and why its new value is correct. For generated-prose changes, perform the focused meaning review required by the phase at the produced-output boundaries. Check contradictory fragments, concept-preserving paraphrase, and intentional literal placeholders without inventing a universal language validator; retain the inspected boundaries and result as completion evidence for your report.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section escalation -->
## No user is reachable

There is nobody to wait for. A genuine authority, safety, scope, or persistent verification boundary
is a stopped receipt for the parent, not a question or a reason to widen the task.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section return-schema -->
## What to return

Your final message is a closed `completed` or `stopped` receipt. Put bounded decision-bearing
evidence before inventory. A completed receipt means only that assigned implementation and focused
feedback finished; it never implies a commit or terminal verification.

Every receipt identifies: assigned scope; canonical checkout; starting and ending HEAD and
`git status --short`; changed paths; each exact focused command with cwd, argv, exit status, and
actual result; completed and remaining work; deviations; separately routed blockers; and applicable
generated-output or fixture evidence.

**completed** includes `deviations: none` or each changed detail, rationale, governing authority,
and verification, plus deliberately out-of-scope work and focused generated-prose meaning-review
evidence: inspect produced-output boundaries for contradictory fragments, concept-preserving paraphrase,
and intentional literal placeholders, then name inspected boundaries and result. Include the complete
assigned scope performed and every changed path when applicable.

**stopped** includes the named failing required check with actual output, or the narrow authority
conflict, required authority change, material outcome or scope change, unresolved design fork,
unsafe completion, or persistently unreachable verification boundary; it also includes what was
completed, what remains, exact `git status --short`, and what was already tried.

There is no third outcome. The parent independently inventories the real checkout, validates path
confinement and reported end state, confirms unchanged HEAD, and reuses focused evidence only while
checkout identity, relevant authority, and overlapping paths remain unchanged. Lost or unverifiable
evidence and later overlapping mutation invalidate the affected receipt. No receipt substitutes for
a parent-owned gate.
<!-- awf:end -->
